      "hints": [
        "Calculate perpendicular distance between parallel lines $x - 2y = 0$ and $x - 2y = 1$: $d = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1^2 + (-2)^2}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\approx 0.45$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express both parallel lines in standard Cartesian form $Ax + By + C = 0$:\n$$\\text{Line } AB: \\quad x - 2y - 1 = 0$$\n$$\\text{Tangent: } \\quad x - 2y = 0$$",
        "Apply the perpendicular distance formula between parallel lines $Ax + By + C_1 = 0$ and $Ax + By + C_2 = 0$:\n$$d = \\frac{|C_1 - C_2|}{\\sqrt{A^2 + B^2}} = \\frac{|-1 - 0|}{\\sqrt{1^2 + (-2)^2}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\approx 0.4472 \\approx 0.45 \\quad (\\text{to 2 d.p.})$$"
